00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.770
PHIL: I've been here for five years
and every year I've worked with many

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.360
young people who are really funny.

00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:15.719
And this specific one, I used to...

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.980
when I was, I used to work one-to-one
with a young man and he was using...

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:29.085
we were using, ABLLS as an
assessment, as an assessment system.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:34.455
One of the main things that we were
working on, one of the reasons we

00:00:34.455 --> 00:00:40.095
were using ABLLS is life skills, we
wanted this beautiful to start to be

00:00:40.095 --> 00:00:42.345
able to say quarter past or half past.

00:00:44.121 --> 00:00:47.385
And so we did a lot of work on that
and it started by, so we use a dry

00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:53.365
wipe clock and write on different
times and, you know, say "Oh, 10:15.

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:54.545
That's quarter-past.

00:00:54.645 --> 00:00:55.005
Right."

00:00:55.425 --> 00:01:00.885
And then maybe write quarter-past
ten as well in words, and then

00:01:01.635 --> 00:01:03.405
expand on that by giving choices.

00:01:03.405 --> 00:01:06.195
Once you've got quarter-past
and half-past separately.

00:01:06.585 --> 00:01:11.895
So, "Oh, it's 10:30, is that
quarter-past 10 or half-past 10?"

00:01:11.895 --> 00:01:13.235
And that takes a bit of work.

00:01:13.235 --> 00:01:15.695
So just give them, you know,
minimal choices, not overwhelm them.

00:01:17.748 --> 00:01:20.340
Not placing too much demand,
not too many choices.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:27.090
And when this particular pupil told me
that it was quarter-past, that 15 on a

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:35.320
digital clock meant quarter-past, and also
that when the big hand is on 3, that means

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.010
a quarter-past,  such was my joy I lept.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.160
I went "yes!"

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:40.139
really loud.

00:01:40.529 --> 00:01:45.915
...that huge achievement, not just
because it ticked the box for me as

00:01:45.915 --> 00:01:51.585
a teacher, but that this person had
got that understanding and now could,

00:01:51.825 --> 00:01:55.485
you know, was beginning to tell the
time that was such, you know, I was

00:01:55.485 --> 00:02:01.305
so overcome with joy that it actually
scared - it made the young person jump.

00:02:02.325 --> 00:02:04.605
So then we had to do a
bit more work after that.

00:02:04.695 --> 00:02:07.555
We actually took a little step
back because I'd made them

00:02:07.575 --> 00:02:11.155
jump because I was so happy.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.095
So that was the one that
always sticks with me.

